1
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:41,000
Death runs in the family.

2
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:16,000
Final Destination Bloodlines is a horror, mystery
film directed by Adam B. Stein.

3
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:51,000
Plagued by a violent recurring nightmare, college student Stefanie heads home to track down the one person who might
be able to break the cycle and save her family from the grisly demise that inevitably awaits them all.

4
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:26,000
Stefani Reyes, played by Kaitlyn Santa Juana.

5
00:22:55,000 --> 00:23:01,000
Charlie Reyes, played by Teo Briones.

6
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:36,000
Darlene Campbell, played by Rya Kihlstedt.

7
00:32:05,000 --> 00:32:11,000
Erik, played by Richard Harmon.

8
00:36:40,000 --> 00:36:46,000
Bobby, played by Owen Patrick Joyner.

9
00:41:15,000 --> 00:41:21,000
Julia, played by Anna Lore.

10
00:45:50,000 --> 00:45:56,000
Final Destination Bloodlines is a 2025 American supernatural horror film directed by Zach
Lipovsky and Adam Stein, and written by Guy Busick and Lori Evans Taylor.

11
00:50:25,000 --> 00:50:31,000
It is the sixth in the Final Destination film series, and stars Kaitlyn Santa Juana as a college student named Stefani Reyes, who inherits visions of a 1969
premonition that averted a deadly skyscraper failure from her dying grandmother Iris, who warns Stefani that Death is coming for their family.

12
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
Teo Briones, Richard Harmon, Owen Patrick Joyner, Anna Lore, Brec
Bassinger, and Tony Todd appear in supporting roles.

13
00:59:35,000 --> 00:59:41,000
After the commercial success of the previous film, a sixth film entered
development, described as a re-imagining of the franchise.

14
01:04:10,000 --> 01:04:16,000
In March 2020, series producer Craig Perry said the film
would be set "in the world of first responders".

15
01:08:45,000 --> 01:08:51,000
In January 2022, the film was scheduled for release on the streaming service HBO Max,
with Lipovsky and Stein directing and Busick joining Taylor as co-writer.

16
01:13:20,000 --> 01:13:26,000
In March 2024, Warner Bros.

17
01:17:55,000 --> 01:18:01,000
Pictures announced that the film would instead receive a theatrical release.

18
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:36,000
Filming took place in Vancouver from March to May 2024,
following delays caused by the SAG-AFTRA strike.

19
01:27:05,000 --> 01:27:11,000
Final Destination Bloodlines was released in the United
States on May 16, 2025, by Warner Bros.

20
01:31:40,000 --> 01:31:46,000
The film received generally positive reviews from critics and grossed $316 million,
becoming both the best-reviewed and highest-grossing installment in the series.

21
01:36:15,000 --> 01:36:21,000
In August 2025, it was announced that a sequel was in development.

22
01:40:50,000 --> 01:40:56,000
The film explores themes of restaurant, gore, sequel, premonition, fate.

23
01:45:25,000 --> 01:45:31,000
The tone is mind_bending and dark and intense.
